  <p style="margin-top:10px;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)">All shown at scale; detail intentionally not legible.</p>

  <h2>One map, four ways through it</h2>
  <p>To understand where the purchase opportunities were for the HEMS products, we needed to understand each journey depending on where the customer started. This led to the multiple journeys that illustrated where those opportunities lived, and what each persona's experience looked like.</p>
  <p>The master blueprint held the whole system; the journeys made it personal. Each detailed journey is a section of the service map pulled out and rebuilt around a specific buyer we'd identified — same underlying machinery, different touchpoints, different order of events.</p>
  <p>Structuring the work around the four personas produced <b>three distinct journeys</b> — HEMS, EV, and one that didn't exist until a customer forced the issue. Some personas share a journey but enter and leave it at different points; some cross from one journey into another mid-stream. <em>Hover a persona to see their path.</em></p>

